# User-facing copy only

Never put developer/ops-facing text in product UI (pages users or operators see as part of the site).

## Do not show in UI

- Shell commands (`pnpm …`, `doppler …`, `wrangler …`, `git …`)
- Env var names (`DATABASE_URL`, `ADMIN_SYNC_SECRET`, …)
- Internal file paths, package names, host/plan internals (`maxDuration`, Hobby vs Pro) unless the audience is explicitly an engineering doc
- “Run X from CLI” / “see docs/…” instructions meant for developers

## Where that content belongs

- `docs/` (e.g. `docs/igdb-sync.md`, `docs/engineering.md`)
- `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, CLI `--help`, code comments
- PR descriptions and commit messages

## UI empty/error states

Speak like a publication, not a setup guide:

- Good: “No games in the catalog yet.”
- Bad: “Run sync from Admin Sync or `pnpm sync:igdb:secrets import --year 2026`.”

Admin/ops screens may describe *what the control does* in plain language. Still no CLI commands or env var names in the rendered UI.
